    # to BM25, which real search engines use. It's TF-IDF plus two
    # improvements: (a) diminishing returns for repeated words (a doc
    # saying "python" 50 times isn't 50x more relevant than saying it
    # once), and (b) length normalization (long docs naturally contain
    # more words, so raw counts unfairly favor them).
